WEBVTT

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.870
Come back!

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.520
Darling, do you hear that whistling?

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:07.520
Ah, it’s Joe!

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.070
What?

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:10.330
Joe, you say?

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.590
Are ya sure?

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.020
Sounds like he's back!

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.030
Hey! Joe’s back! He’s over there!

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.880
This smell sure takes me back!

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.830
The filth does too!

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.450
Hey, Joe.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.370
Hurry up, will ya.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.380
Don’t be so stiff. It's been a while since I've been back to these slums.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:44.530
Joe!

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.350
Joe!

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:46.810
Joe!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.280
Long time no see!

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.270
My, my, Joe!

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.310
What’s happening with you?

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.040
You look well!

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.010
Thank you, thank you.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.360
Sorry for being away for so long.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.670
Say, when did you come back?

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.130
Looks like you’ve gotten a size bigger!

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.900
Oh my, he’s so much more mature-looking now.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.330
He sure is a handsome man now.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.360
But he looks a little underfed.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.340
Yeah, well, I doubt juvie is a good place to get a decent bite to eat.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.540
By the way, where are the kids?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.450
Like Tarou, Sachi and the rest?

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.650
Leave the exchange of pleasantries for later!

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.970
There’s something I wanna show to you right away!

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.380
Come, come, come, come.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.230
Aren’t you Yabuki Joe?

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.350
Well, Mr. Officer, thank you for helping me out back then.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:33.360
Now, now, I'm just glad I turned you around.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.000
Now, now, just thank your officer friends for knocking my senses into me.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.970
Cut it out, Joe!

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.500
Hey, that hurts, old man!

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.470
How much farther are you gonna drag me?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.790
That should be enough.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.860
Now, take a look under the bridge.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.620
What’s supposed to be down there?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.770
T-Tange Boxing Club.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.560
T-Tange Boxing Club.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.020
Yes, Tange Boxing Club.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:27.640
So that you and I can punch our way back into Japan's boxing world.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.330
It's going to be our beloved headquarters!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.670
Kinoko!

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.850
He… He’s finally back!

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:39.980
Bro Joe is here!

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:39.980
<i>What?</i>

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.630
Joe!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.260
Joe!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.130
Welcome back!

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.290
Joe!

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.060
Welcome back!

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.330
Bro!

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.120
Tonkichi, right?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.490
Yeah, Bro!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.320
And you’re Hyoromatsu.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.690
Bro!

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:13.400
Sachi.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.200
Hey, Bro. Welcome back, my lord.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.920
You did your long sentence commendably.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.000
I’ve always wanted to say that!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.010
This is just like in the movies, Joe, when the criminal is finally released from jail!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.150
You kids…

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.010
You kids sure have grown a lot.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.240
Let me see, Sachi.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.450
Cut it out.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:36.610
You’re embarrassing me.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.480
You’ve gotten so heavy.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.770
How embarrassing.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:43.870
You too, Kinoko.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.150
That tickles!

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.490
Hyoromatsu as well.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.960
I think you’re a heavyweight now.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.540
I’m so flattered!

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.570
If I hold someone like you, Tarou, it’ll be a disaster.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:04.880
Sorry, but no.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:11.640
Joe!

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.240
Step inside and take a look.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.680
It’s your gym.

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:45.470
Do ya like it?

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:46.640
Isn’t is wonderful, Joe?

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.100
Wow, it’s even got a ring.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.100
This place is a little cramped, but there's still room to practice.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.880
Hey, hey, Joe, come on, look at that.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.360
“Mammoth Nishi”?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.440
Mammoth!

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.270
Mammoth is back, everyone!

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:09.380
Mammoth!

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.740
Joe, you’ve finally shown yourself, eh?

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.830
So “Mammoth” was…

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.040
referring to you?

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.290
Everybody's got a nickname now, like Fighting Harada or Strongman Fujikura.

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:23.760
So you mean…

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.800
You’re also going to be a pro boxer?

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:26.960
Yeah.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.330
The boxing bug possessed me while I was in the prison.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.950
Well, I’m not sure how far I can go.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.980
But let me tell ya, my main reason for taking up boxing is <i>you</i>, Joe.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.270
It’s because of you!

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.100
Me?

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.650
If I keep up boxing, it means I won’t have to say goodbye to you.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.650
Well, not like that really matters.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:48.160
I have to apologize for not coming to meet up with you sooner.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.570
But I’m a full-fledged clerk at a grocery store.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:58.580
Nishi-kun is using all his earnings to get the equipments for this gym.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.770
D-Don’t say it like it’s such a big deal, old man.

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:03.560
Old man, it's actually…

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:03.560
<i>It’s not “old man,” Mammoth!</i>

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.630
Call him Chief! Chief.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.060
Ah, sorry.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:10.020
I was trying to say that the Chief works all day as a laborer,

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:11.790
often working three to five times harder than everyone else!

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.600
You keep quiet, Nishi-kun.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.600
Adults can't have a real conversation with Joe.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.640
That's why he needs us kids to make things easier.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.680
See, see, look at this! I sewed this mitt by myself!

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.530
And bro, take a look at the sandbag!

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:30.790
The sandbag too!

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.150
Hyoromatsu and I made it.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.660
Lemme borrow you for a sec.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.040
I’m gonna show you something nice.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.170
Something really nice.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.170
Oh, there’s even a shower room?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.910
We thought that after you worked up a huge sweat practicing,

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.550
you’d want to take a nice, refreshing shower.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:57.180
And, to explain this highly sophisticated Kinoko-brand shower mechanism-

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:57.180
<i>Joe!</i>

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.180
Don’t listen to him. Just pull that string, okay?

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.100
You mean this?

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.100
Oh no…

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.300
Sachi, you idiot!

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:12.990
I figured something like this would happen.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.360
Sorry!

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.690
Sorry, Joe.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:17.330
Hello!

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:20.830
Um, excuse me, but can you tell me where the Tange Boxing Club is?

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.680
Hey, hey! You're silly!

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:25.330
Where do you think you’re looking?

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:26.910
Eh?

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:28.420
How did that get there?

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.710
Did you bring more equipment?

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.340
I brought flowers.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.440
Flowers!

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:48.970
Perfect!

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:51.520
Someone sent us this to celebrate the club's grand opening!

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.820
You jackass!

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.240
That’s a wreath for <i>funerals</i>.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.100
Hey, sir, isn’t there some sort of mix-up?

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.530
What a sick joke!

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.130
He’s right!

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.240
If you don’t scram quick, I’ll throw my getas at ya!

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.730
Yes, but I was instructed to…

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:05.840
Never mind your instructions, what does that note say? That one there.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.320
“To the Tange Boxing Club Wannabes.”

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:17.760
<i>Who</i> is behind this!?

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.880
They ruined our excitement.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.570
Who would <i>dare</i> send this to us?

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:38.340
Tell me.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:39.710
Who is the guy who ordered this wreath?

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.910
I... I took a phone call.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.040
From a guy named “Rikiishi.”

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.010
R-Rikiishi?

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.310
R-Rikiishi?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.660
That bastard…

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:54.000
Um, excuse me, is there a Yabuki-san here?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:54.810
There is.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.260
What business have you got with Bro Joe?

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:57.730
He has a phone call.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:58.760
A phone call.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.560
Phone call?

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.020
I’m in no mood to deal with that now!

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:02.120
I’ll call them back!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.720
Who is it?

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.220
Um, some guy named Rikiishi…

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:10.730
Rikiishi?

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:13.360
Joe!

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:26.190
R-Rikiishi?

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:27.210
R-Rikiishi?

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.250
Why you…

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:31.280
Hi there, Yabuki.

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:33.250
You did your long sentence commendably.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.260
What’s the big idea sending me that wreath?

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:37.110
What of it?

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:40.260
I'm just cooling that hot head you developed in juvie.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.260
The “Tange Boxing Club Wannabes.”

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.260
Do you understand the meaning behind it?

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.960
That means you're just a pretend club

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:51.270
that's not officially recognized by the JBC.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.270
Which also means that a pro like me…

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.020
isn’t allowed to play around with you.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.370
What did you say, you jackass?

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:00.480
Blah-blah-blah-blah!

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.530
Rikiishi, quit yapping on the phone and c'mere!

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:08.540
Sorry, but unlike you I am quite busy these days.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.540
Fine. If you won’t come to me then I’ll come to you!

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:16.050
He sure acts up fast.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:19.930
Rikiishi-kun…

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:23.360
You mustn’t take off during practice without permission.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.390
Your trainer is looking for you.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.920
My apologies, Miss.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.390
I just had something to say to this strange guy.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:32.980
“Strange guy”?

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:37.140
It’s no big deal.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:38.990
Well, I’m returning to practice now.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.440
Where do you think you’re going?

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:48.490
Where are you going, Joe!

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.600
Isn’t it obvious? Yohko’s house!

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.750
If I go there, I’m sure someone’ll know where her pet Rikiishi is!

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:54.660
No, don’t do it, Joe!

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:55.790
You can’t do reckless things like this!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.040
Stop it, Nishi!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.250
You trying to stop me?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.470
No! I’m not trying to stop you.

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:02.340
I just…

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.760
I’m just warning you that picking a fight with Rikiishi right now won’t solve anything!

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.170
Shut up!

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.260
That guy's got me pissed as hell!

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.020
Idiot!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.840
This place isn’t the juvenile prison!

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.570
It’s proper society!

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:24.700
Who'd think that you, the former jail boss,

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.180
would become such a damn goodie-goodie.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:32.590
Oh, Nishi.

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:35.040
You put out some pretty nice punches.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.880
Did my punches surprise you?

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.630
You ain't seen nothin' yet!

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:43.140
You jerk.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:45.010
Now you're getting full of yourself.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.720
Hey, that’s not fair using your weight like that!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.180
You idiot!

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:54.680
Shit.

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:57.690
Joe, you idiot!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.430
Joe, you idiot!

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:00.190
You idiot!

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:10.720
If you want to get even with Rikiishi…

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.800
Then you should fight him properly in the ring-

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:13.350
Shut up!

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:14.170
Get off!

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.120
You and your big, ugly face!

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.910
Get off, I said!

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:24.500
Joe, the outside world is harsh.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.050
What’s with you, Nishi?

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.620
All you’ve been talking about today is society this and the outside world that.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.010
You’ve lost your mind, man.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:32.960
Ouch.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.020
That body blow really got me.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:42.860
Everything you taught me at the prison...

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.270
That’s where I learned to punch like that.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:47.870
Do you think Rikiishi, the self-named prodigy,

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:51.580
was taking it easy while waiting for you to get out?

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:03.090
I… I get it.

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:04.450
I… I get it.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:10.510
Nothing to cry over, right?

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.630
I… I’m sorry… Joe

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:34.650
Joe!

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:36.650
Joe!

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.150
Bro Joe!

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:40.090
Bro Joe, they’re having a party!

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.450
A party!

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:44.510
A welcome back party, they say!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.060
Thank you, townsfolk. Please, come on in!

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.410
If everyone will please...

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:07.500
...come in.

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:08.070
Ouch!

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:10.500
Oops, sorry!

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:11.750
My bag ripped.

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:13.070
I brought my winnings from Pachinko with me.

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:15.770
This one’s <i>mine</i> !

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:30.400
They’re really at it!

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:33.840
Darn it, why did I have to get this blasted shift?

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.420
Drink up, drink up, Chief.

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:00.540
You’ve really put yourself through hell for a while to help us.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:12.460
You really did give yourself a hard time there.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.090
Oops, oops, oops…

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.890
Thanks for that.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:23.170
Yummy!

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:31.660
I’ve always wanted to eat an entire can of these, all by myself, just once…

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.530
He's just eating crab meat.

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.670
The scale is just so small, my goodness!

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:38.240
Look who’s talking, Sachi. You’ve been sucking on that dried squid forever now.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.540
Oopsie, you’re right.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:43.080
Go, go, go!

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.510
What’s wrong with that guy?

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:47.280
He accidently drank some sake, thinking it was water!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.980
Hey, where’s Joe?

00:17:57.730 --> 00:17:59.330
Where’s that jackass, Joe?

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:01.520
Where is he?

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.560
Sitting over there.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.920
That's great! You're doing great!

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:48.790
Joe.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:58.710
You wanna know something about this bridge?

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:01.950
People call it the “Bridge of Tears.”

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:06.630
Where people’s dreams are shattered by life.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.550
And when they get exhausted with their lives,

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:11.400
all those sorts of people flow here to Slum Town.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:14.360
They cross over this sad bridge with tears in their eyes.

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:16.460
I was one of those people three years ago.

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.430
And you were supposed to be one of them too.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:20.620
But…

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:24.730
This time you and I will cross this “Bridge of Tears” with laughter.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:28.430
Because I want us to take the first step towards tomorrow’s splendor!

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.310
Do you understand?

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.760
Do you understand the meaning behind what I’m saying?

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:31.390
Huh?

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:33.940
Do you understand what I’m telling you, Joe?

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:36.770
I do understand… sort of.

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:39.950
But, please, there’s no need to be so melodramatic about it.

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:41.860
Towards tomorrow…

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:45.130
No, towards the world of pro boxing.

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.450
If you want to work towards that, there will be hard times and suffering.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:52.180
And you might have to shed even more tears than you’ve shed thus far.

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.080
But!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.840
They won’t be the tears of a loser.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.660
They will be for the glory of fighting through harsh times towards the splendor.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.860
They will be brilliant, sweaty tears!

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:03.170
So, Joe, let’s suffer together.

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:04.810
Let’s grit our teeth together.

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:07.710
And let’s cross this Bridge of Tears going the <i>opposite</i> direction!

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:32.920
This party’s <i>boring</i> without the guest of honor!

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:35.500
Hurry back!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:39.110
See? Everyone is celebrating your rebirth.

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:40.800
Let’s go back in. Okay?

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.170
I can’t walk too well.

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:46.000
Oh dear, oh dear.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.470
Oops, oops, oops…

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:53.300
Cross the Bridge of Tears… in the <i>opposite</i> direction, eh?

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:03.680
What a shame.

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:06.170
I know I'm supposed to be on duty…

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:09.020
but they sure picked a hell of a time for my shift.

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:51.140
This is the first time in my life…

00:22:52.330 --> 00:22:54.840
The first time I've had a hard time sleeping.

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:58.090
This really is the first time in my life.

00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:00.730
Why do I feel so uneasy right now?

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:11.930
It’s the first time it’s ever happened to me!

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:36.230
Embraced in the love of those around him, Joe cried.

00:23:36.230 --> 00:23:38.330
The tears that sparkled on Joe’s cheeks,

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:40.630
those were tears of joy.

00:23:40.630 --> 00:23:45.020
However, Guerrilla suddenly appears, threatening his newfound happiness.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:46.770
Enticing Joe to join them on a journey.

00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:51.040
Now, for Joe, who is taken by the Law of the Stray Dog,

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:53.030
which way is tomorrow!?
